#!/usr/bin/env bash
# UserPromptSubmit: put the reply-format, chain-of-command and screenshot rules in front of Claude on every owner message.
in=$(cat)
echo "REPLY FORMAT (CLAUDE.md): this is the owner's own message. Line 1 of your reply is 🔴 NEEDS YOU: <ask> (ask first, options + recommendation up top) or 🟢 DONE: <result> (only if fully done with no question, offer or pending choice; otherwise 🔴). 🔴 only for a real ask only the owner can answer or do, never 'nothing' as the ask. If nothing is needed from the owner but work is still in flight (CI running, merge pending, waiting on another session), tag it ⚙️ AUTO: <what is done, what is being waited on>. Turns you are woken for later (CI, watcher, background task, peer) are ⚙️ AUTO: max 2 lines unless it carries the What I did summary; a real unanswered ask is repeated as the last line: ⏳ Still waiting on you: <ask> (never 'nothing'; no open ask means omit it). If this message asks for a change, feature or fix, add a short 'What I did:' summary under the tag line (2-5 plain bullets: how you understood the request, what you implemented, anything left out or done differently; for a fix or 'something is wrong', also the logic BEFORE that caused the problem and what it is NOW)."
echo "CHAIN OF COMMAND (CLAUDE.md standing rule): the Deploy Manager (session titled exactly \"🚀 Deploy manager (typecast)\"; find its id with list_sessions, ignore titles starting \"💀 (retired)\"; the title is the lookup key) alone owns the deploy/CI/process mechanisms: DEPLOYING.md, CLAUDE.md standing rules, .claude/ hooks and settings, CI workflows, deploy/watch/smoke scripts, notifications. If the owner asks a feature session to add or change any of those, do NOT edit them yourself: send the request, in the owner's words, to the manager with mcp__claude-code-remote__send_message, tell the owner in one line that you passed it on, and carry on with your feature work (the manager has a worker make the change). Your own feature code, tests and docs/features/* still go through the normal branch + PR flow. Exception: the owner says in the same message that you should edit it directly."
echo "SCREENSHOT RULE (CLAUDE.md 'Screenshots for visual changes'): if the owner sent a screenshot or complained about a look, OR you choose the visuals yourself (layout, colours, spacing, icons, animation, new UI), OR the owner asked for a specific design, your reply MUST include a screenshot of the result (same view/viewport/data; before/after for a complaint). Skip it, with one line saying why, only for a tiny request whose exact visual result the owner dictated, or a change with no visible effect. One command: node scripts/shot.mjs \"/path\" [--click TEXT] [--sel CSS] [--phone] --out <scratchpad>/x.png, then SendUserFile; one view, look once, prefer --sel, no loops."
exit 0
